---
import { customers, products, orders, items, payments } from './model.mjs';
const groups = [
 ['customers', ['customer_id · PK', 'name'], customers],
 ['orders', ['order_id · PK', 'customer_id · FK', 'status'], orders.filter(r => r[0] === 103).map(r => [r[0],r[1],r[3]])],
 ['order_items', ['order_id · PK/FK', 'line_no · PK', 'product_id · FK', 'quantity', 'unit_price'], items.filter(r => r[0] === 103)],
 ['products', ['product_id · PK', 'name', 'price', 'stock'], products.map(r => [r[0],r[1],r[2],r[0] === 'P3' ? 10 : r[0] === 'P7' ? 0 : r[3]])],
 ['payments', ['payment_id · PK', 'order_id · FK', 'amount', 'method'], payments]
];
---
<figure class="relational-figure shop-rows">
 <p class="figure-title">One order connects several kinds of fact</p>
 <p class="legend">PK = primary key; FK = foreign key. Values shown after order 103 is accepted. Amounts are pounds.</p>
 <div class="key-flow" aria-label="Key relationships"><span>customers</span><b>1 → many</b><span>orders</span><b>1 → many</b><span>order_items</span><b>many → 1</b><span>products</span></div>
 <div class="key-flow"><span>orders</span><b>1 → many</b><span>payments</span></div>
 {groups.map(([name, columns, rows]) => <div class="relation"><table><caption>{name}</caption><thead><tr>{columns.map(c => <th>{c}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{rows.map(row => <tr>{row.map(v => <td>{v}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div>)}
 <figcaption>Figure 1. Illustrative shop data after order 103 is accepted. PK marks columns forming the primary key; FK marks a foreign key. Labels show how many rows on either side can correspond; foreign-key values identify the referenced rows. A customer can have no orders, and an order can have no lines or payments. The order and line tables show only 103; payments show earlier orders 101 and 102. Amounts are pounds. This view omits dates and historical rows, not additional stock reservations.</figcaption>
 <details><summary>Read this figure as text</summary><p>Mina Shah is customer 1. Her pending order 103 has two lines: one blue mug P7 at £20.00 and two green teas P3 at £4.50 each. Its value is £29.00 and it has no payment. Stock is now zero mugs, ten teas and four teapots. Earlier payments 501 and 502 settle order 101; 503 settles order 102. Tariq Aziz and Edda Berg retain customer identities 2 and 3.</p></details>
</figure>
<style>
 .shop-rows .figure-title{margin-top:0;font-weight:700}.shop-rows .legend{font-size:.8rem}.shop-rows .relation{overflow-x:auto;max-width:100%;margin:1rem 0}.shop-rows table{display:table;width:100%;margin:0;font:.78rem/1.5 var(--font-mono)}.shop-rows caption{text-align:left;font-weight:700;padding:.4rem 0;color:var(--color-text)}.shop-rows th{white-space:nowrap}.shop-rows th,.shop-rows td{padding:.45rem}.key-flow{display:flex;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.45rem;font-size:.8rem;margin:.5rem 0}.key-flow span{border:1px solid var(--color-rule);padding:.3rem}.key-flow b{font-size:.7rem;font-weight:400}.shop-rows details{font-size:.85rem}
</style>
